1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:06,466
Beyond login, Privy holds a robotics lab's money.

2
00:00:06,496 --> 00:00:09,334
The lab's budget is a Privy server wallet, under a

3
00:00:09,364 --> 00:00:11,435
policy with one allowed action:

4
00:00:11,465 --> 00:00:15,383
a transaction to Thenar's contract on Monad testnet,

5
00:00:15,413 --> 00:00:17,541
worth at most a tenth of a MON.

6
00:00:17,721 --> 00:00:19,421
Here it posts a bounty.

7
00:00:19,451 --> 00:00:24,111
Privy signs, and Monad executes it and makes it final.

8
00:00:24,141 --> 00:00:26,503
Then the same wallet is asked to send money to another

9
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:29,986
address, and Privy's policy engine refuses before a

10
00:00:30,016 --> 00:00:31,541
signature exists.

11
00:00:32,221 --> 00:00:34,338
An operator picks up the lab's task.

12
00:00:36,868 --> 00:00:39,613
And one Monad transaction records their run and pays

13
00:00:39,643 --> 00:00:42,179
them from the escrow the Privy wallet funded.

14
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:46,044
Operators sign in with Privy too, and get paid into that wallet.

15
00:00:46,724 --> 00:00:49,260
A lab can automate bounties, and the worst case is that

16
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:51,163
it funded Thenar tasks.

